      "title": "Background Work and Caching: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Background Work and Caching: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The request path rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Keep the response ==fast==",
                "Push slow or non-essential work off the request: emails, reports, webhooks",
                "==Cache== repeated reads instead of recomputing them"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three tools, one guard",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Runs in",
                "Durable?",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**BackgroundTasks**",
                  "web process",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "fire-and-forget"
                ],
                [
                  "**Task queue**",
                  "separate worker",
                  "{green:yes}, retryable",
                  "heavy, critical jobs"
                ],
                [
                  "**Cache**",
                  "Redis",
                  "until TTL",
                  "computed responses"
                ],
                [
                  "**Rate limiter**",
                  "Redis counters",
                  "per window",
                  "reject the excess"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rate limiting counts requests per ==key== (IP, user, API key) in a time window",
                "The excess gets HTTP ==429=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Redis is the shared backbone",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "cards",
              "spec": {
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "title": "Celery",
                    "lines": [
                      "broker",
                      "result store"
                    ],
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "ARQ",
                    "lines": [
                      "job queue"
                    ],
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Cache",
                    "lines": [
                      "computed responses"
                    ],
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Rate limits",
                    "lines": [
                      "counter store"
                    ],
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**BackgroundTasks vs queue?** BackgroundTasks for quick, loss-tolerant work; a queue for durable, retryable, heavy jobs",
                "**What is 429?** Too Many Requests; the `Retry-After` header tells the client when to retry",
                "**Why Redis, not memory?** Memory is per process and lost on restart; Redis is shared by every worker"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "BackgroundTasks and Its Limits",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "BackgroundTasks and Its Limits",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Usage",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Add a ==BackgroundTasks== param to the route",
                "`add_task(fn, arg, kw=val)` queues the call",
                "Runs ==after the response== is sent, in the **same process**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.post('/signup')",
                "async def signup(background_tasks: BackgroundTasks):",
                "    background_tasks.add_task(send_email, to, subject='Hi')",
                "    return {'ok': True}"
              ],
              "note": "the client gets the response first"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Where it runs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Runs on",
                "Risk"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`def`",
                  "threadpool",
                  "uses a pool thread"
                ],
                [
                  "`async def`",
                  "event loop",
                  "{red:blocking call freezes the whole server}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:No durability}: crash, deploy or restart loses pending tasks",
                "No retries, no result retrieval, no status tracking",
                "Exceptions after the response are only **logged**, never seen by the client",
                "Shares the web worker's ==CPU and memory=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Outgrown it?",
              "text": "Move to a ==queue== when you need retries, durability or status, or when jobs are long, critical or CPU-heavy."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Task Queues: Celery vs ARQ",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Task Queues: Celery vs ARQ",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Flow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "API",
                    "sub": "enqueues message",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "Redis / RabbitMQ",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Worker",
                    "sub": "pops and runs",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Result",
                    "sub": "backend or Redis key",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Celery vs ARQ",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Celery",
                "ARQ"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Model",
                  "sync-first, ==beat==, heavy config",
                  "async-native, ==Redis-only==, minimal"
                ],
                [
                  "Enqueue",
                  "`fn.delay(x)`, `apply_async(countdown=, retry=)`",
                  "`await redis.enqueue_job('fn', x)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Define",
                  "`@app.task`",
                  "`async def fn(ctx, x)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Run",
                  "`celery -A proj worker -l info`",
                  "`arq module.WorkerSettings`"
                ],
                [
                  "Safety",
                  "`acks_late`, `max_retries`",
                  "`max_tries`, `job_timeout`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.task(acks_late=True,",
                "  autoretry_for=(IOError,),",
                "  retry_backoff=True, max_retries=5)",
                "def send(user_id): ..."
              ],
              "note": "Celery reliability settings"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Delivery is ==at-least-once==: make tasks **idempotent**",
                "Pass ==IDs==, not objects: args must serialize",
                "Never block the API on `.get()`",
                "Set time limits, concurrency, visibility timeout > longest task"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Choose?** Async FastAPI on Redis: ARQ; schedules, RabbitMQ, features: Celery",
                "**At-least-once?** A task may run twice, so it must be idempotent",
                "**Status?** Return a job ID; client polls a status endpoint"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
