    {
      "title": "Redis Response Caching and Invalidation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Redis Response Caching and Invalidation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cache-Aside and Keys",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Build key",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "GET",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hit: return",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Miss: compute",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SET EX ttl",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Key holds ==every input== that changes the output, including user",
                "Store **JSON** strings",
                "Never cache personalized data under a shared key"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "async def cached(page, uid):",
                "    key = f\"v1:products:list:page={page}:user={uid}\"",
                "    raw = await r.get(key)",
                "    if raw: return json.loads(raw)",
                "    data = await load(page, uid)",
                "    await r.set(key, json.dumps(data), ex=60)",
                "    return data"
              ],
              "note": "fragment: r is a redis.asyncio client"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Invalidation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Strategy",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "TTL expiry",
                  "simplest"
                ],
                [
                  "`DEL` on write",
                  "after DB commit, not before"
                ],
                [
                  "Version / prefix bump",
                  "`v1` → `v2`"
                ],
                [
                  "`SCAN MATCH prefix*`",
                  "groups; never `KEYS`"
                ],
                [
                  "Write-through",
                  "write cache and DB together"
                ],
                [
                  "Write-around",
                  "write DB only; fill on read"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Stampede and HTTP",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Jitter== on TTLs stops mass expiry (avalanche)",
                "Hot key expires: lock with `SET NX EX`; others wait or serve stale",
                "`ETag` lets the client revalidate and get 304",
                "`Cache-Control` for client caching; cache only GET and 2xx"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Order",
              "text": "Commit the DB first, then `DEL`; the reverse re-caches stale data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rate Limiting with slowapi and Redis Counters",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rate Limiting with slowapi and Redis Counters",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. slowapi Setup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "limiter = Limiter(key_func=get_remote_address, storage_uri=\"redis://...\")",
                "app.state.limiter = limiter",
                "app.add_exception_handler(RateLimitExceeded, handler)",
                "@limiter.limit(\"5/minute\")",
                "async def ping(request: Request): ..."
              ],
              "note": "request param is required"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No `storage_uri`: counts live in ==memory per process==",
                "Several workers: limits break; {green:Redis} shares counts"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Counter Algorithms",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Edge",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fixed window",
                  "double burst",
                  "`INCR` + `EXPIRE`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sliding window",
                  "smooth",
                  "sorted set"
                ],
                [
                  "Token bucket",
                  "smooth",
                  "allows bursts"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Make it ==atomic==: Lua script, or `SET NX EX` + `INCR`",
                "Separate `INCR` and `EXPIRE` can leave a key with **no TTL**",
                "Limit hit: {red:429}; `Retry-After` needs `headers_enabled=True`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Behind a proxy, `get_remote_address` sees the ==proxy IP==",
                "Read `X-Forwarded-For` only from a **trusted proxy**",
                "Prefer a user or API-key key",
                "Redis down: decide ==fail-open== or ==fail-closed=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Fixed vs sliding vs bucket?** Fixed is simple but bursts at the edge; others smooth",
                "**Why fail with workers?** Each process counts alone",
                "**Limit hit?** 429 plus `Retry-After`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
